invariant: INV-38
file: Makefile
catches: test/tx-record-builds.sh
reason: the Makefile stops refusing TX_RECORD beside
  TRANSPORT=quic-nonblocking and writes -DCH_TX_PT into a QUIC object's
  defines. session.h still stops a raised value at the first source, with
  a static assertion rather than the axis's own message, and
  TX_RECORD=512 builds a QUIC object whose defines and variant directory
  name a setting it never reads.

--- old
ifeq ($(TRANSPORT),quic-nonblocking)
$(error TX_RECORD=$(TX_RECORD) sizes a TLS record, and TRANSPORT=quic-nonblocking seals none: drop TX_RECORD, or use TRANSPORT=tcp-blocking or TRANSPORT=tcp-nonblocking)
endif
--- new
